## ⚠️ Security Note

The Anthropic API key is used client-side in this demo for hackathon purposes. For production:

1. Create a simple backend proxy (Express/Next.js API route)
2. Move all `fetch("https://api.anthropic.com/...")` calls there
3. Store the key server-side only

Example Next.js API route:
```js
// pages/api/roast.js
export default async function handler(req, res) {
  const response = await fetch("https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "x-api-key": process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, // server-side only
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
      "anthropic-version": "2023-06-01"
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(req.body),
  });
  res.json(await response.json());
}
```

